/test
/meeting
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyodu

# Version model repos from external apps. 
/model_repos/

# REAL Allianz artefacts. These patterns were anchored at the repo root (/data/real/) but the
# directories are src/data/real/ and src/models/real/, so NOTHING was ignored — on the company
# laptop the real exports would have been committable. Corrected 2026-08-18.
src/data/real/**
src/models/real/

# ...with ONE exception: the data dictionary. It documents the columns of artefacts that only
# exist on the company laptop, so it is useless unless it travels there — and it carries no data,
# only column names and grains. The directory itself must NOT be excluded (git cannot re-include
# a file under an excluded directory), which is why the rule above ends in `**`.
!src/data/real/DATA_MODEL.md

# The local dummy stand-in lives at src/data/real/ too and is covered by the rule above. It is
# not committed on purpose: regenerate it with `python src/data/make_dummy_real.py`, which IS
# tracked. Committing fake data to the same path the real exports occupy is how the two get
# confused.

# Feature registries (features/registry/<v>.json). DERIVED per machine, by running
# features/extract_features.py (v2/v3) or extract_features_v1.py (v1) against that machine's own
# pickles — so the company laptop's are the real ones and a local file is a shape stand-in. Same
# reasoning as src/data/real/ above, with one edge that makes it sharper: the sync is one-way
# (local -> company), so a local stand-in committed here would OVERWRITE the real registry on
# arrival, and the real one cannot come back. The directory and its README stay tracked.
features/registry/*.json
features/registry/_DUMMY_REGISTRY
# Same for the mapping it validates: feature_overlap.json is BUILT by check_overlap.py from
# the Excel sheet, which lives only on the company laptop. A local stand-in must not travel.
features/feature_overlap.json

# Per-version envs (src/envs/v{1,2,3}/.venv). Built per machine — the company laptop's are the
# real ones, a local one is a path-resolution stand-in.
src/envs/*/.venv/ 